<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">
<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<body class="portal-legal-body">
  <header class="portal-legal-header">
    <a href="/login" class="portal-legal-brand" aria-label="Findoly provider login">
      <img src="/images/findoly-logo.png" alt="Findoly">
      <span>Provider portal</span>
    </a>
    <a class="btn btn-light btn-sm" href="/login">Provider login</a>
  </header>

  <main id="policy-top" class="portal-legal-shell">
    <article class="card portal-legal-card">
      <div class="card-body">
        <span class="portal-legal-kicker">Findoly Solutions LLP</span>
        <h1>Grievance Redressal Policy</h1>
        <p class="portal-legal-lead">How Provider Portal complaints are submitted, acknowledged, investigated, resolved and escalated.</p>
        <p class="portal-legal-effective">Effective and last updated: 30 July 2026</p>
        <aside class="portal-legal-callout is-important"><strong>Email-only grievance channel</strong><p>Submit Provider Portal grievances to support@findoly.com. Never email OTPs, UPI PINs, CVV or full card numbers.</p></aside>
        <nav class="portal-legal-toc" aria-label="Contents of Grievance Redressal Policy">
          <strong>On this page</strong>
          <ol>
          <li><a href="#purpose">Purpose and scope</a></li>
          <li><a href="#contact">Grievance contact</a></li>
          <li><a href="#categories">Types of grievances</a></li>
          <li><a href="#required-information">Information to include</a></li>
          <li><a href="#acknowledgement">Acknowledgement and reference</a></li>
          <li><a href="#review">Review process</a></li>
          <li><a href="#resolution">Resolution timelines</a></li>
          <li><a href="#urgent">Urgent safety, security and unlawful-content cases</a></li>
          <li><a href="#privacy">Privacy grievances</a></li>
          <li><a href="#payments">Payment grievances</a></li>
          <li><a href="#lead-data">Lead-data misuse complaints</a></li>
          <li><a href="#appeal">Request for reconsideration</a></li>
          <li><a href="#external-remedies">External remedies</a></li>
          <li><a href="#records">Records, confidentiality and abuse</a></li>
          <li><a href="#updates">Policy updates</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <div class="portal-legal-content">
<section id="purpose">
  <h2>1. Purpose and scope</h2>
  <p>This policy provides a single process for Provider Portal complaints concerning account access, payment verification, credits, lead-data misuse, privacy, intellectual property, unlawful content, security and other Platform matters. It does not replace urgent emergency reporting or a statutory remedy.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="contact">
  <h2>2. Grievance contact</h2>
  <p><strong>Designated contact:</strong> Grievance Officer, Findoly Solutions LLP<br><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a><br><strong>Address:</strong> Findoly Solutions LLP, WeWork Mindspace, 6th Floor, Malad West, Mumbai – 400064, Maharashtra, India.</p>
<p>Findoly currently accepts Provider Portal grievances by email. No telephone grievance channel is published.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="categories">
  <h2>3. Types of grievances</h2>
  <ul><li>Login, OTP, eligibility or account suspension.</li><li>Payment debited but digital delivery not completed.</li><li>Duplicate credit deduction or transaction discrepancy.</li><li>Privacy access, correction, erasure or security concern.</li><li>Misuse of customer lead information or unwanted Provider contact.</li><li>Copyright, trademark, impersonation or unlawful content complaint.</li><li>Technical access or material service issue.</li><li>Appeal against a moderation or enforcement decision.</li></ul>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="required-information">
  <h2>4. Information to include</h2>
  <ul><li>Full name, business name and registered Provider mobile number.</li><li>Email address from which you can receive the response.</li><li>Clear description of what happened and the outcome requested.</li><li>Relevant dates, order IDs, payment references, lead references or URLs.</li><li>Supporting screenshots or documents with payment secrets removed.</li><li>Whether the issue creates an immediate safety, fraud or data risk.</li></ul>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="acknowledgement">
  <h2>5. Acknowledgement and reference</h2>
  <p>Findoly will acknowledge a grievance within the period required by applicable law. Where the Information Technology intermediary grievance timeline applies, the target is acknowledgement within twenty-four hours. The acknowledgement may request missing information and may include a case or request reference.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="review">
  <h2>6. Review process</h2>
  <p>The case may be routed to support, billing, security, privacy, marketplace operations, legal or another relevant team. Findoly may review account records, transaction logs, lead activity, communications, vendor status and information supplied by affected parties.</p>
<p>The complainant must cooperate with reasonable verification. Incomplete, abusive or unverifiable complaints may be delayed or closed with reasons.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="resolution">
  <h2>7. Resolution timelines</h2>
  <p>Findoly will resolve or respond to grievances within the period required by applicable law. Where the current general intermediary grievance timeline applies, the target is resolution within fifteen days from receipt. Certain categories may have shorter legal timelines, and payment or bank-dependent cases may require an interim response while external confirmation is pending.</p>
<p>A response may confirm correction, explain why no correction is due, request further evidence, notify an interim protective measure or identify an external process.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="urgent">
  <h2>8. Urgent safety, security and unlawful-content cases</h2>
  <p>Clearly identify an urgent risk in the subject line. Findoly may preserve evidence, restrict access or content, suspend an account, notify affected users or cooperate with lawful authorities. Do not use the grievance email as a substitute for police, emergency, bank fraud or cybercrime reporting when immediate action is required.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="privacy">
  <h2>9. Privacy grievances</h2>
  <p>Privacy requests should use the subject “Privacy Request” and identify the requested access, correction, erasure or concern. Findoly may verify identity and may retain records where legally required. Information about another person may be redacted.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="payments">
  <h2>10. Payment grievances</h2>
  <p>Payment complaints should use the subject “Payment Review” and include the gateway reference, date, amount and expected entitlement. Resolution follows verified gateway and Platform records and the Cancellation and Refund Policy. Do not send OTPs, UPI PINs, CVV or full card numbers.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="lead-data">
  <h2>11. Lead-data misuse complaints</h2>
  <p>A Customer or Provider reporting unwanted contact, resale, disclosure or misuse should identify the relevant communication and, where known, the Provider or lead reference. Findoly may restrict access while investigating serious misuse.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="appeal">
  <h2>12. Request for reconsideration</h2>
  <p>If you believe a decision overlooked material evidence, reply to the grievance response with the reference and the specific new or misunderstood information. Repeated submissions without new information may be closed.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="external-remedies">
  <h2>13. External remedies</h2>
  <p>Nothing in this policy prevents a person from using a court, payment-provider process, data-protection mechanism, consumer forum, cybercrime channel or other authority where legally available. Findoly may require exhaustion of its grievance process before an internal appeal, but cannot remove a non-waivable statutory right.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="records">
  <h2>14. Records, confidentiality and abuse</h2>
  <p>Findoly may retain grievance records for investigation, audit, security, legal claims and compliance. Information is shared internally and externally only as reasonably necessary. Threats, spam, false evidence, impersonation and abusive duplicate complaints are prohibited and may lead to restriction or legal action.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section><section id="updates">
  <h2>15. Policy updates</h2>
  <p>Findoly may update this process when law, designated personnel, categories or operational systems change. The latest version will be published on this page.</p>
  <a class="portal-legal-back-link" href="#policy-top">Back to contents</a>
</section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="portal-legal-navigation" aria-label="Policies and support">
      <strong>Policies and support</strong>
      <%- include('../partials/policy-links', { policyLinksClass: 'portal-policy-links' }) %>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="portal-legal-page-footer">
    <span>© <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> <%= legalEntityName %></span>
    <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
